                        "language": "english",
                        "review": "Suprisingly fun (given its low price point), colorful twin-stick shooter with a rich passive 'buffs' tree, and a variety of characters you can play as with different ranged/weapon specialties and unlocks, and a unique special attack/ability for each character. Some interesting variations in enemy AI behavior, and some interesting environmental hazards. A sprint/roll ability adds some movement variety.\nhttp://steamcommunity.com/sharedfiles/filedetails/?id=966085428\nhttp://steamcommunity.com/sharedfiles/filedetails/?id=966073516\nKilling enemies drops green credits that you can pick up and use between levels to improve passive buffs. You get credits even if you die on a level. And this is *not* a roguelike/roguelite, so you keep your progression through the 60 handcrafted levels.\n\nI haven't gotten far enough yet to try all the special abilities. One provides a protective shield around you. Another casts a sort of spell on surrounding enemies so that they take each other for a time. Another freezes nearby targets temporarily.\n\nSo far I prefer the Deep Waker Zero character for his bullet-hell like SMG weapon, which is so far what I have the most fun using in this. :)\nhttp://steamcommunity.com/sharedfiles/filedetails/?id=966072352\nCons? imho, it's held back a bit imho by lack of terrain variety, absence of any interesting objectives (it's clear the map and find the portal) and generally very rudimentary sound FX. Which probably is just a function of a small budget. I think the basic twin-stick gameplay -- though I'm playing on kb/mouse -- is generally spot-on. :)\n\nThis is an Early Access title, so it'll be interesting to see how it evolves.",
